    "field": "Glaciology",
    "problem": "Estimating the Greenland Ice Sheet's mass loss before 1992 is challenging due to a lack of direct, Greenland-wide observations, forcing reliance on models and creating a significant gap in observation-based estimates for twentieth-century sea-level rise budgets.",
    "method": "The authors propose a method to calculate spatial ice mass loss from the Greenland Ice Sheet since 1900 using a geodetic approach based on aerial imagery to map geomorphic features related to its maximum extent during the Little Ice Age.",
    "task": "The task is to calculate the spatial and temporal distribution of ice mass loss from the Greenland Ice Sheet since 1900 using historical aerial imagery to map geomorphic features related to its maximum extent at the end of the nineteenth century.",
